// The "acid keeps eating away until scraped off" lingering-damage rider IS
// modeled, via `damage_effect: Some(Buff(...)))` applying the existing
// Burning BuffKind (common/src/comp/buff.rs) as a damage-over-time tick --
// Burning is implemented purely as a HealthChangeOverTime effect, making it
// the closest existing generic DoT primitive regardless of its fire-coded
// name (the same kind of buff-kind reuse the Necromancy batch already
// established for e.g. ray_of_sickness reusing Sickened).
//
// BasicBeam also hardcodes DamageKind::Energy in
// common/src/states/basic_beam.rs (no RON-configurable damage_kind field
// exists on this variant) -- true in-engine base-tick damage is Energy,
// not Acid, flavor-only mismatch; the DoT rider is still real acid-style
// health drain regardless of its BuffKind's fire-coded name.
BasicBeam(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    beam_duration: 5.0,
    damage: 6.0,
    tick_rate: 2.0,
    range: 9.0,
    max_angle: 5.0,
    damage_effect: Some(Buff((
        kind: Burning,
        dur_secs: 4,
        strength: DamageFraction(0.15),
        chance: 0.5,
    ))),
    energy_regen: 0,
    energy_drain: 8,
    move_efficiency: 0.3,
    ori_rate: 0.3,
    specifier: Poison,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
